\NewDocumentCommand{\uname}{s+m} {
    \seq_clear:N \itemname_wue% these are not supposed to build beyond 1. Thats probably why I made them token lists when I first did it.  I dont remember the reason I wanted to change them into sequences for ocd reasons. They remain token lists in warhammerweaponentry, which is probly why that doesnt have the same issue. This is really two problems at once, because the crappy solution for interface999 calling both uname and wname at once. I never noticed it until now because some how for reason I do not understand at all, if you encapsulate stuff in either minipages or multicols (which I do for the armoury stuff) insulates things after it. Maybe that is a nuance to environments as a core part of latex?
